{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-skein-generation","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:skein-generation","kind":"proposition","title":"The skein module of the 3-sphere is free on the unknot","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-hadron-operations","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-hadron-fibre-embedding"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-skein-generation"],"cites":["references/lickorish1997"],"tags":["skein","generation","homflypt"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Torsion.skein_generation","text":"skein-generation.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:skein-generation\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R = \\mathbb{Q}(a, q)</code> and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Sk}(S^3)</code> be the skein module of oriented links in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S^3</code> over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>: the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module spanned by isotopy classes of oriented links, modulo the HOMFLYPT skein relation</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  a\\, L_+ - a^{-1} L_- = (q - q^{-1})\\, L_0</code></pre>\n<p>for every triple <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(L_+, L_-, L_0)</code> of links that differ only at one crossing. Then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Sk}(S^3)</code> is free of rank one, spanned by the unknot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  [L] = P_L(a, q)\\,[U]</code></pre>\n<p>for every oriented link <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L</code>, where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_L \\in R</code> is the HOMFLYPT polynomial normalised by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_U = 1</code>. In particular every link, and so every hadron configuration of <a href=\"#rem:hadron-operations\" data-at=\"knots-particles-confinement/hadron-algebra\">9.3.8</a>, has a terminal skein resolution: a finite reduction of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L</code> to a multiple of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U</code>.</p>\n<p>The specialisation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a = 1</code> is the relation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_+ - L_- = (q - q^{-1}) L_0</code> of the corpus's Hecke–skein convention, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_L</code> is then the Conway polynomial in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = q - q^{-1}</code>. At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a = q</code> every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_L</code> equals <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code>, so that specialisation carries no information about <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L</code>. The reading of this resolution in terms of torus knots, the Hopf link and hadron masses is in <a href=\"#rem:skein-generation-hadron-reading\" data-at=\"mass-theory/mass-algebraic-consolidated/mass-algebraic-transfer-skein\">13.4.11</a>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-generation.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.4.9","page":"b/prop-skein-generation","qa":{"counts":{"pass":90,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":79},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.LiftingDescent.skein_generation","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/skein_generation.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
